import TechIcons from "./SvgSection.astro";

---



<div class="relative text-container mt-10 ">
  <h2 class="xl:text-5xl text-2xl w-2/4 z-50 font-bold m-0">Technologies, frameworks &</h2>
  <h2 class="xl:text-8xl text-5xl text-accent font-bold">Dev Languages</h2>
</div>
<div class="my-10 xl:mr-20">
  <p class="xl:text-xl serif">
    I'm a <strong *class="font-bold">Frontend Developer</strong> with a
    full-stack background and a strong interest in building, evolving, and
    improving digital products. Throughout my career, I've worked across
    different technologies, frameworks, and environments, from modern
    applications to <strong *class="font-bold">legacy systems</strong>, always
    adapting the stack to the needs of the project rather than being tied to a
    single technology.
  </p>

  <p class="xl:text-xl mt-3 serif">
    My strongest experience is in <strong *class="font-bold">frontend
    development</strong>, particularly with Angular and TypeScript, while my
    background also includes JavaScript, Node.js, React, Next.js, and backend
    development. Alongside traditional software development, I've built
    automation tools, APIs, scrapers, and applications integrating
    <strong *class="font-bold">AI services such as the OpenAI API</strong>.
    More recently, my work has increasingly focused on
    <strong *class="font-bold">AI-assisted software development</strong>,
    exploring agent skills, structured workflows, and approaches such as
    <strong *class="font-bold">Spec-Driven Development (SDD)</strong> with
    tools such as Claude.
  </p>

  <p class="xl:text-xl mt-3 serif">
    I enjoy working at the intersection of <strong *class="font-bold">software
    development, automation, and AI</strong>, with a practical mindset and a
    focus on solving real problems. Whether I'm working on a new Angular
    application, evolving a legacy codebase, or exploring how AI can improve
    the development process, I aim to understand the bigger picture and build
    solutions that are maintainable, useful, and genuinely effective.
  </p>
</div>



